statement:
Let $\alpha$ be a finite field, let $n$ and $k \ge 1$ be natural numbers, and fix a nonzero codeword $x \in \alpha^{k}$ together with an integer $d > 0$. Regard an $n \times k$ matrix $G$ over $\alpha$ as chosen uniformly at random among all $\abs{\alpha}^{nk}$ such matrices, so that the image $Gx$ is a codeword of length $n$. Then the probability that $Gx$ has Hamming weight strictly less than $d$ is at most the fraction of all codewords of length $n$ that lie in the Hamming ball of radius $d-1$ about the all-zero codeword:
\[
\frac{\abs{\{\, G \in \alpha^{n \times k} : \operatorname{wt}(Gx) < d \,\}}}{\abs{\alpha}^{nk}}
\;\le\;
\frac{\abs{B_{d-1}(\mathbf{0})}}{\abs{\alpha}^{n}}.
\]
